5. API Request & Response (10 Important APIs)

The backend wraps every response in: { success, statusCode, message, data, meta? } (meta omitted when not paginated).

1. POST /api/v1/auth/register
   Purpose: Register a new account and send OTP verification
   Auth: None | Role: Public
   Validation: name (min 3), email, role (CUSTOMER | TECHNICIAN), password (8-40 chars, ≥1 uppercase, ≥1 lowercase, ≥1 number, ≥1 special char)
   Request Body:
   {
     "name": "Rahim Uddin",
     "email": "rahim@example.com",
     "role": "CUSTOMER",
     "password": "StrongPass123!"
   }
   Successful Response (200):
   {
     "success": true,
     "statusCode": 200,
     "message": "Register  OTP send successfully",
     "data": null
   }
   Possible Error Response:
   {
     "success": false,
     "statusCode": 409,
     "message": "User with this email already exists",
     "data": null
   }

2. POST /api/v1/auth/login
   Purpose: Sign in and issue JWT tokens (accessToken + refreshToken set as httpOnly cookies)
   Auth: None | Role: Public
   Request Body:
   {
     "email": "rahim@example.com",
     "password": "StrongPass123!"
   }
   Successful Response (200):
   {
     "success": true,
     "statusCode": 200,
     "message": "User logged in successfully",
     "data": {
       "user": { "id": "user_123", "name": "Rahim Uddin", "email": "rahim@example.com", "role": "CUSTOMER", ... },
       "accessToken": "jwt_access_token",
       "refreshToken": "jwt_refresh_token"
     }
   }
   Possible Error Response:
   - 401: "Invalid credentials"
   - 404: "User not found"
   - 403: "User is blocked" / "User is deleted"

3. GET /api/v1/auth/me
   Purpose: Get current user profile
   Auth: Required (Bearer token) | Role: ADMIN, CUSTOMER, MANAGER, SUPER_ADMIN, TECHNICIAN
   Successful Response (200):
   {
     "success": true,
     "statusCode": 200,
     "message": "User profile fetched successfully",
     "data": {
       "id": "user_123",
       "name": "Rahim Uddin",
       "email": "rahim@example.com",
       "role": "CUSTOMER",
       "emailVerified": true,
       "status": "ACTIVE",
       "customer": { ... }                        // CUSTOMER only
       // TECHNICIAN: technician { regions, availability[{startTime, endTime (HH:mm)}], skills[{category}] }
       // MANAGER: manager { region }
     }
   }
   Possible Error Response:
   {
     "success": false,
     "statusCode": 401,
     "message": "Unauthorized",
     "data": null
   }

4. POST /api/v1/service/
   Purpose: Create a service request and auto-create a linked WorkOrder (status SCHEDULED)
   Auth: Required (CUSTOMER)
   Validation: title, description (min 5), servicingDate (not in past), address (object), categoryId, regionId (uuid), priority, optional preferredStartTime/preferredEndTime (HH:mm)
   Request Body:
   {
     "title": "AC Maintenance",
     "description": "Indoor AC not cooling properly.",
     "servicingDate": "2026-11-15",
     "address": { "street": "House 12", "area": "Mirpur", "city": "Dhaka" },
     "categoryId": "d0f54a0d-3ce2-44c2-bb7a-7f8ac8a7ef99",
     "priority": "HIGH",
     "regionId": "84d19316-1f50-4d85-a3d0-b87f4aa1c574",
     "preferredStartTime": "10:00",
     "preferredEndTime": "12:00"
   }
   Successful Response (200):
   {
     "success": true,
     "statusCode": 200,
     "message": "service request retrived successfully",
     "data": {
       "id": "svc_456",
       "title": "AC Maintenance",
       "description": "Indoor AC not cooling properly.",
       "servicingDate": "2026-11-15",
       "address": { "street": "House 12", "area": "Mirpur", "city": "Dhaka" },
       "duration": 120,
       "categoryId": "d0f54a0d-3ce2-44c2-bb7a-7f8ac8a7ef99",
       "priority": "HIGH",
       "regionId": "84d19316-1f50-4d85-a3d0-b87f4aa1c574",
       "preferredStartTime": "10:00",
       "preferredEndTime": "12:00",
       "status": "PENDING",
       "customerId": "cust_001",
       "customer": { ... },
       "workOrders": [{ "id": "wo_123", "servicingDate": "2026-11-15", "status": "SCHEDULED", "customerId": "cust_001", "regionId": "..." }],
       "createdAt": "...",
       "updatedAt": "..."
     }
   }
   Possible Error Response:
   {
     "success": false,
     "statusCode": 400,
     "message": "Validation failed",
     "data": null
   }

5. GET /api/v1/service/my-services
   Purpose: Get all service requests for the current customer
   Auth: Required (CUSTOMER)
   Successful Response (201):
   {
     "success": true,
     "statusCode": 201,
     "message": "service retrive successfully",
     "data": [
       {
         "id": "svc_456",
         "title": "AC Maintenance",
         "status": "PENDING",
         "servicingDate": "2026-11-15",
         "category": { "id": "...", "name": "..." },
         "workOrders": [{ "id": "wo_123", "technician": { "user": { ... } } }]
       }
     ],
     "meta": { "total": 1, "page": 1, "limit": 9, "totalPages": 1 }
   }
   Possible Error Response:
   {
     "success": false,
     "statusCode": 404,
     "message": "No service requests found",
     "data": null
   }

6. POST /api/v1/service/assign-technician
   Purpose: Assign a technician to an existing work order and update its status (also creates bKash payment)
   Auth: Required (MANAGER)
   Request Body:
   {
     "workOrderId": "9f8fa4ee-8e5d-42ed-9e01-6cc0d197d9d7",
     "technicianId": "ab2357b9-4cc3-4f66-9d84-7e83d19f5e9b",
     "amount": 5000,
     "status": "ASSIGNED"
   }
   (status: "REJECTED" or "ASSIGNED"; amount required for bKash payment creation)
   Successful Response (200) — status ASSIGNED:
   {
     "success": true,
     "statusCode": 200,
     "message": "Technician assigned successfully",
     "data": {
       "id": "9f8fa4ee-8e5d-42ed-9e01-6cc0d197d9d7",
       "servicingDate": "...",
       "status": "EN_ROUTE",
       "technicianId": "ab2357b9-4cc3-4f66-9d84-7e83d19f5e9b",
       "managerId": "...",
       "serviceId": "svc_456",
       "service": { "id": "svc_456", "status": "ASSIGNED", "category": {...}, "region": {...} },
       "customer": { ... },
       "technician": { "user": { "id": "...", "name": "...", ... } },
       "schedule": {...},
       "payment": {...}
     }
   }
   When status is "REJECTED": message "Service rejected successfully", WorkOrder status CANCELLED, returned data is the updated Service.
   Possible Error Response:
   {
     "success": false,
     "statusCode": 409,
     "message": "Technician is unavailable for this date",
     "data": null
   }

7. GET /api/v1/workorder/:workOrderId
   Purpose: Fetch a single work order
   Auth: Required (ADMIN, CUSTOMER, MANAGER, SUPER_ADMIN, TECHNICIAN)
   Successful Response (200):
   {
     "success": true,
     "statusCode": 200,
     "message": "work order retrive successfully",
     "data": {
       "id": "9f8fa4ee-8e5d-42ed-9e01-6cc0d197d9d7",
       "servicingDate": "2026-11-15",
       "status": "EN_ROUTE",
       "note": null,
       "serviceId": "svc_456",
       "customerId": "cust_001",
       "technicianId": "ab2357b9-4cc3-4f66-9d84-7e83d19f5e9b",
       "managerId": "...",
       "regionId": "...",
       "service": { "id": "svc_456", "...", "category": {...} },
       "customer": { "user": {...} },
       "technician": { "user": {...} },
       "manager": { "user": {...} },
       "schedule": {...},
       "payment": {...},
       "feedback": {...},
       "attachment": [...],
       "serviceReport": {...},
       "createdAt": "...",
       "updatedAt": "..."
     }
   }
   Possible Error Response:
   {
     "success": false,
     "statusCode": 404,
     "message": "Work order not found",
     "data": null
   }

8. PATCH /api/v1/workorder/update
   Purpose: Update work order status
   Auth: Required (TECHNICIAN)
   Request Body:
   {
     "workOrderId": "9f8fa4ee-8e5d-42ed-9e01-6cc0d197d9d7",
     "status": "STARTED"
   }
   (status: "STARTED" | "COMPLETED"; not allowed from SCHEDULED, not EN_ROUTE→COMPLETED, not CANCELLED/COMPLETED)
   Successful Response (200):
   {
     "success": true,
     "statusCode": 200,
     "message": "work order status successfully",
     "data": { /* full formatted work order as in #7 */ }
   }
   Possible Error Response:
   {
     "success": false,
     "statusCode": 400,
     "message": "Invalid status transition",
     "data": null
   }

9. POST /api/v1/payment/create
   Purpose: Create a bKash payment request for a service
   Auth: Required (CUSTOMER)
   Preconditions: service IN_PROGRESS/COMPLETED, workOrder not CANCELLED/EN_ROUTE, payment not already PAID
   Request Body:
   {
     "workOrderId": "9f8fa4ee-8e5d-42ed-9e01-6cc0d197d9d7"
   }
   Successful Response (200):
   {
     "success": true,
     "statusCode": 200,
     "message": "payment url created successfully",
     "data": {
       "paymentID": "pay_222",
       "amount": "...",
       "currency": "BDT",
       "bkashURL": "https://sandbox.bkash.com/payment/pay_222",
       "status": "...",
       "merchantInvoiceNumber": "...",
       ...
     }
   }
   (data is the raw bKash checkout/create response; paymentUrl = bkashURL)
   Possible Error Response:
   {
     "success": false,
     "statusCode": 400,
     "message": "Payment cannot be created for this work order",
     "data": null
   }

10. POST /api/v1/feedback/
    Purpose: Create customer feedback after service completion
    Auth: Required (CUSTOMER)
    Preconditions: workOrder and service COMPLETED, payment PAID, customer owns workOrder, no existing feedback
    Request Body:
    {
      "workOrderId": "9f8fa4ee-8e5d-42ed-9e01-6cc0d197d9d7",
      "rating": 5,
      "comment": "Excellent service and punctual response."
    }
    Successful Response (201):
    {
      "success": true,
      "statusCode": 201,
      "message": "feedback created successfully",
      "data": {
        "id": "fb_101",
        "workOrderId": "9f8fa4ee-8e5d-42ed-9e01-6cc0d197d9d7",
        "rating": 5,
        "comment": "Excellent service and punctual response.",
        "createdAt": "...",
        "updatedAt": "...",
        "workOrder": { "...", "technician": {...} }
      }
    }
    Possible Error Response:
    - 500: "You have already reviewed this service work"
    - 400: "without complete you can not crate review" / "you can not feedback before payment"

6. Basic Backend Architecture

High-Level Flow
Client → API → Route → Controller → Service → Repository / ORM → Database

Layer Responsibilities
- Client: Web/mobile app or API consumer that sends HTTP requests.
- API Layer: Receives requests, exposes endpoints, and routes them to the proper controller.
- Route Layer: Maps URL patterns and HTTP methods to controller functions.
- Controller: Validates input format, handles request parsing, and passes data to services.
- Service Layer: Contains core business logic such as user authorization, service eligibility checks, scheduling validation, assignment logic, and payment validation.
- Repository / ORM Layer: Executes database queries using Prisma ORM or direct data access methods.
- Database: PostgreSQL stores users, service requests, work orders, technicians, ratings, payments, and reports.

Where Security and Validation Happen
- Authentication occurs in middleware before controller logic through JWT verification.
- Role-based authorization is checked in the middleware or service layer for restricted routes.
- Request validation is performed using Zod schemas or validation middleware.
- Error handling is centralized in a global error handler to return consistent JSON responses.
- Logging and auditing can be implemented in middleware or through dedicated services.

External Integrations
- Cloudinary for file upload and attachments.
- bKash payment gateway for payment creation and callback handling.
- Redis for caching and performance optimization.
- Nodemailer for email OTP and verification messages.
- PDF generation for service summaries or reports when needed.

